  "OverallSummary": "This case involves Park Avenue Securities LLC (PAS) failing to establish, maintain, and enforce a supervisory system and written supervisory procedures (WSPs) reasonably designed to achieve compliance with suitability requirements regarding mutual fund share class recommendations to retirement plan customers. From January 2019 through July 2021, PAS failed to properly supervise these recommendations, violating FINRA Rules 3110 and 2010. Additionally, from June 30, 2020 (when Reg BI went into effect) through July 2021, PAS violated the Care Obligation and Compliance Obligation under Reg BI by failing to consider costs associated with different mutual fund share classes when making recommendations to retirement plan customers.\n\nSpecifically, PAS's supervisory system and WSPs failed to provide guidance for evaluating whether Class A or Class C shares were in the best interest of retirement plan customers when they were eligible to purchase Class R shares. This failure affected 355 retirement plan customers who purchased Class A or C shares when Class R shares would have been more beneficial, causing these customers to incur $91,344.52 in either unnecessary front-end sales charges (Class A) or higher operating fees (Class C). The Care Obligation violation stemmed from PAS's failure to properly consider costs associated with different share classes and recommend the most cost-effective option for retirement plan customers. PAS has paid restitution to the affected customers and was censured and fined $125,000 by FINRA. The firm had previously been sanctioned for similar issues related to mutual fund sales charge waivers in July 2019 and by the SEC in March 2019."
